  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile+avgpool substantially outperforms singleprofile (0.485) and transformer aggregation (0.519). However, PCA is the only RNA encoder tested, leaving a major uncertainty: whether a learned representation (scvi_n200) can improve upon PCA in the same multiprofile+avgpool setting. Question: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares to config_002 by changing only the RNA encoder, cleanly isolating the representation effect while holding the best-performing profile and aggregation fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: It tests the most impactful untested design variable (encoder) in the context of our strongest configuration. If scvi_n200 matches or beats PCA, it validates learned representations and opens the door to scgpt and multimodal extensions. If it underperforms, it tells us PCA is surprisingly competitive and we should focus budget on other axes (image, fusion). Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about which encoder to build further upon, making this the highest-information-per-experiment choice under budget constraints."
}

